WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.580
♪ ...don't know who she is ♪

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.370
♪ Or how she is ♪

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.710
♪ Or when, what, why she is ♪

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:30.710
♪ But as for where she is, she is where we will go ♪

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:34.130
♪ To Adelaide! ♪
♪ To Adelaide! ♪

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.890
♪ Come on and join the Adelaide parade♪

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:37.640
- No.
- No.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.010
♪ Adelaide! ♪

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.640
♪ To Adelaide! ♪

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.920
♪ Let's go to Adelaide's house ♪

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.750
I need to fix that last part,

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.060
but that's the idea.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.820
So, Beatrice, you sing you sing the high parts

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.860
Wirt, you sing the really high part.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:52.400
What?

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.270
Oh.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.990
- And...
- Nobody is singing anything anymore.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.490
And, Wirt, keep moving.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.490
But I-I have to...

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.160
...ugh.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.010
Alright.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.500
- But we have to do something fun.
- You know, we really don't.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.080
We can just keep walking silently, you know?

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.540
And... ugh.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.260
Wirt, let's go. Come on.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.340
Sorry, sorry.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.500
But shouldn't we...

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.380
Greg, don't you want to be more like your brother?

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.360
...just always doing what you're told.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:15.840
Huh?

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.040
...just a pathetic pushover to make all his decisions.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.140
Hey! What? I'm not a pushover.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.850
Hold on, Wirt. Let me get to my point.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.100
Ugh, fine.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:27.520
See, Greg? No willpower whatsoever

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.520
Hrmph!

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:29.860
You need to be more like that.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.360
But that doesn't really sound that fun.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.570
The world is a miserable place, Greg.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.950
Life isn't fun.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.120
Then I'll do what I need to do, I guess.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:39.620
Thank you.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.820
We'll just focus on getting you guys to Adelaide's

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.300
so I can wash my hands of this whole affair.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.890
And if you could pick up the pace a bit,

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.580
that'd be great, okay?

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:49.630
Okay?

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:50.920
Hey, where's Greg?

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.630
Oh. Uh, wondered off, I guess.

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:54.800
Cheese and crackers!

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.800
We need to do our part to make the world a better place!

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:58.890
Graawr

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.220
Ha ha, yeah.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.140
Huh? Whoa!

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:05.910
School?!

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.890
Pssh! Not today.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.900
Greg!

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.940
Greg! Greg?

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.320
Oh.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.820
- Greg?
- Excuse me?

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.980
Please, take your seat, children.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.830
You're late.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.080
You know the rules...

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.410
"once the bell has rung, class has begun."

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.990
Oh, sorry, everybody. Sorry.

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.240
No, he doesn't have a brain. He can't learn anything.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.050
Let's go, Wirt. Come on. Here, boy.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.610
What? Did you say something?

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.210
I can't hear you because I'm too busy doing what I'm told.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.730
What? What are you...

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:40.750
No, no. Let's go.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.240
Oh, no. See, I'm a pushover, remember?

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.680
I have to do what she tells me to do.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.680
ugh...

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.350
Wirt, your brother could be in trouble somewhere.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.020
tap, tap, tap, tap

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:54.020
Mnh-mnh-mnh, mnh-mnh.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.110
Ha ha! Yeah!

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.400
Bluebird's have a short life span.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.260
You two are literally killing me

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.950
every moment I'm forced to spend with you.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:04.730
Oh.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.210
Young man, I will not stand for such nonsense in my classroom.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.980
I've got enough nonsense from that

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.960
no good, two-timing, low-down, handsome man of mine.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.300
Oh, Jimmy Brown, why did you have to leave me so?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.540
And now, with my father threatening to close the school

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.080
and that wild gorilla on the loose,

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.880
why, Jimmy, I just have one thing to say...

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.890
♪ "A" is for the apple that he gave to me ♪

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:34.560
♪ but I found a worm inside ♪

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.320
♪ "B" is for beloved that♪

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.150
♪ I called to him before... ♪

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.150
Ouf. That lady's got some baggage.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:39.990
What's that?

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:43.820
Young man, go to the dunce box.

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:44.990
Oh. Sure!

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.160
- Okay! sure.
- No, no. No, no, no.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.080
[ Wirt Humming ]

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.080
Aw.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.080
Now, where were we?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.080
Oh, yes.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.420
♪ "G" is for the gentleman I thought he was ♪

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.420
♪ when he first said hi... ♪

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.760
So, my theory is

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.340
hot dogs are not actually dogs,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.720
regardless of what they teach you in school.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.590
But you guys don't go to school, huh?

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.770
I'm gonna stick with you guys.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.190
Ha ha!

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.060
Hey, I got an idea.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.800
Let's play two old cat.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.030
Do you guys know how to play two old cat?

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.950
It's fun. I'll show you.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.620
Here we go.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.890
Here's one old cat.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:27.950
Meowr

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.540
Mrowr

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:30.790
You found another one!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.710
Wait. No.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.210
I think that cat is too old.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.210
Mrrrowwr

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.130
Sorry, kitty. We'll have to find another old cat.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.300
Hey, Jeffrey, I think there's one behind you!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.760
RaaAAAGH

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.100
Gorilla!

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.640
Run!

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.640
♪ ...and "Y", yes "why"♪

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.560
♪ is the question that's on my mind ♪

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.230
♪ Oh why... ♪

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.360
Hey, dunce! This is dreadful!

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.070
Good, I'm glad you feel that way.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.250
Hmph

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:03.570
Ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.840
♪ ...I remember life with y- ♪

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:03.570
Ahpf!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.150
Huh! Gorilla!

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.740
Raaaaagh

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.160
Mealtime already?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.410
Well, come along children.

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:21.090
Ow!

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.380
We don't want to be late for mealtime.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:27.470
My father will be visiting today,

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:30.560
and we'll need to be on our best behavior.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.310
Quick! In here!

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.060
Oh, boy! Mealtime!

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.230
This is way better than being chased by a gorilla.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.490
Aw, what's the matter?

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.860
Mm. Kind of bland.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.500
Hey, nobody ordered you to eat yet.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.500
Yeah, but...

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:02.590
Ohh.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.970
Hey! I know what to do!

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.180
Here Ms. Langtree, Play something like this.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.760
Oh, like this?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.400
Mm... good enough.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.730
♪ oh, potatoes and molasses ♪

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:26.150
♪ if you want some, oh, just ask us ♪

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:29.200
♪ they're warm and soft like puppies and socks ♪

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.490
♪ filled with cream and candy rocks ♪

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:36.080
♪ oh, potatoes and molasses ♪

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.170
♪ they're so much sweeter than algebra class ♪

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.900
♪ if your stomach is grumblin' ♪

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.900
♪ and your mouth starts mumblin' ♪

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:44.090
♪ there's only one thing ♪

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.880
♪  to keep your brain from crumblin' ♪

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.340
♪ oh, potatoes and molasses ♪

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:52.680
♪ if you can't see 'em put on your glasses ♪

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.020
♪ they're shiny and large like a fisherman's barge ♪

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.020
♪ you know you eat enough when you start seeing stars ♪

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:02.690
♪ oh, potatoes and molasses ♪

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:06.110
♪ it's the only thing left on your task list ♪

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.150
♪ they're short and stout, ♪

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:08.900
♪ They'll make everyone shout! ♪

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.780
♪ for potatoes ♪

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:13.990
♪ and molasses ♪

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.200
♪ for potatoes and... ♪

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.910
-That's enough!
- Father!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:24.590
Is this what I've been paying for?!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:27.090
Hey! We just wanted to have a little fun.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:30.420
I didn't invest in this school for "fun".

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:34.100
I thought we were trying to do important work here

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.350
teaching animals to count and spell.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.520
We are! Oh, please, father, don't close the school.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.940
It won't happen again.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.520
I should say it won't.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:44.980
- This...
- Pbht!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.190
...this...
- Meow!

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:49.860
...and this are all coming with me.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.280
Now send them to bed!

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.370
You heard father. Off to bed with you.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.590
I just wanted to have fun,

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.890
change the world, and make it a better place.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.930
But I just made everything worse.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:18.350
Ruh Raow

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.770
Okay, Wirt, I'll admit it ...

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:21.890
you seem like a pushover,

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.730
- but you're not.
- Oh?

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.020
Deep down in your heart,

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.080
you're a stubborn jerk!

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.160
When are going to give this up?!

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.070
Maybe never. Maybe I'll never give this up.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.070
Hmm...

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.400
Yeah!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.490
Wirt's right! Never give up!

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:34.490
Come on, Wirt.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.410
Let's go save the day.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:37.960
Okay, if you say so!

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:38.660
pfft

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:39.660
Come on.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.670
So, what's the plan, Greg?

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:44.710
Plan?

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.710
- Ohh. I don't know.
-Oooooww

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.090
Who would've thought making a

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.800
primer school for animals was a bad idea?

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.300
My life savings, my home...

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.040
everything I had went into that dear, dear school.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:04.500
And now I'm forced to sell these instruments just to keep it open.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:07.490
All the while that loathsome Jimmy Brown

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:09.820
is off gallivanting who knows where!

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.440
Not to mention that wild gorilla on the loose.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:19.390
If only something would go right for a change.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.950
Zzzzzz

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.820
Okay, I think he's asleep.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:25.460
Let's go steal his stuff.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.920
- What?
- What?

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.460
The instruments!

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:37.250
They've been stolen!

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.510
Who would do such a thing?!

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:40.760
Huh?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.100
- Here you go.
- Oh, here you go, sonny.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.060
What is this?

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.840
It's a benefit concert for the school.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.070
Haah, isn't it grand.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:57.820
All these fine people giving out of the goodness of their hearts?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:00.950
Not like my Jimmy Brown.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.370
Oh, here we go.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.710
All he ever did was steal my heart away.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.790
Gorilla!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.450
Young man, do something!

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.060
Uh...

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.510
Whoa!

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:20.510
- Huh!
- Huh!

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.850
Ugh... finally!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.010
Jimmy?

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.400
That's right, darlin'.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:27.100
I was the gorilla.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.100
But why did you do it?

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.520
Got a job in the circus so's I could finally buy ya that wedding ring.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.420
But when I got stuck in the dang suit,

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:37.400
everybody was too doggone scared to help me out.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.120
Oh, Jimmy.

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.280
- Oh!
- Darlin'.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:41.700
Yeah!

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.180
I guess the world really is as sweet

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:50.210
as potatoes and molasses.

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:53.920
♪ Oh, potatoes and molasses ♪

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.710
♪ if you want some... ♪

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.720
So, want me to tell Greg it's time to get going?

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.470
Nah, let him have his fun.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.390
♪ ...filled with cream and candy and rocks ♪

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.950
- Hey, Wirt.
- Yeah?

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:09.390
- Tie your shoe.
- Hmm? Oh. Mm. Okay.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.110
♪ ...algebra class ♪

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.980
♪ if your stomach is grumblin' and your mouth... ♪

